# Prior for average rate of evolution -- v2 variant, floor lowered 1e-3 -> 1e-6.
#
# Why: the good-238 76-PC run put 90.2% of its sigma2 posterior within 1% of the
# 1e-3 floor, and even the 38-PC run's minimum (0.00112) cleared it by only 12%.
# The v2 tangent-PCA basis is computed on a different taxon set, so sigma2's
# scale shifts and the floor would bite at a different, unknown threshold.
#
# NOT prior-neutral: dnLoguniform is uniform on the log scale, so widening from
# 3 decades to 6 means half the prior mass now sits below 1e-3, where previously
# none did. This mildly favours low rates. Acceptable here because sigma2 is not
# reported and node ages were shown robust to a floored sigma2 on well
# tip-calibrated trees (2026-07-24). It would matter under a relaxed clock.
sigma2 ~ dnLoguniform(1e-6, 1)
moves.append( mvScale(sigma2, weight=1.0) )
